  "adjudication": [
    "L3 is the smallest frozen layer-storage representation with zero reduction-induced aliases at 0.25x, 0.5x and 1x in the candidate-enriched 41-state common cohort.",
    "L3, L4 and L6 have identical alias counts and future-response extrema at every frozen radius in this cohort; extra L4/L6 storage state therefore has no demonstrated state-information value here.",
    "L2 is materially more informative than same-dimension U2 but retains purpose-relevant ambiguity and 1x bottom-flux sign mismatches.",
    "Active-lower-zone placement strongly outperforms same-dimension uniform or near-uniform placement.",
    "Current-profile reconstruction improves from L3 to L4, but A1 shows no corresponding future-response information gain; reconstruction error is not a state-sufficiency acceptance variable.",
    "Together with prior DYN0A evidence that L4 greatly improves standard-LARE propagation over L3, A1 sharpens the attribution toward closure/resolution error rather than missing predictive state information."
